From f3ec6fd95613298b3271c93179da14fdaff56cc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iitimii <timiiowolabi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 11:18:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] V1: verify mode - expert-verified front drafting with
 seq_cp checkpointing

Front drafts k tokens (adaptive 4..24); expert judges them in one batched
forward pass with per-position logits. seq 1 checkpoints the hybrid state
(recurrent seq_cp is copy-on-write) so rejection can roll back what the
Gated-DeltaNet layers cannot rewind. Cross-vocab at text level with
whitespace seams. Acceptance: logprob threshold or greedy argmax match.
Adaptive repair spans; expert can end the turn at any accepted boundary.
Router --hard-mode verify|expert dispatches hard prompts either way;
default expert (measured draft acceptance 0.32-0.42 on this model pair is
below verify break-even ~0.55).

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
